    "body": "### Summary\n\nAdds a granular `disableKnowledgeContext()` switch on `HarnessAgent.Builder` that suppresses the `## Domain Knowledge` guidance, `knowledge/KNOWLEDGE.md` and the knowledge file catalog, while leaving `AGENTS.md`, `MEMORY.md` and the memory tools intact. The approach is sound and the backward compatibility is handled properly — the 6-arg constructor delegates with `false`, and the IO short-circuit in `buildWorkspaceSection` avoids the `readKnowledgeMd()` read entirely rather than reading and discarding. `mergeable` is clean and `Check License` / `Check Module Sync` are green (build still running at review time).\n\nThree things keep this from an approve:\n\n1. **Subagents don't inherit the switch.** `HarnessAgentBuilderSupport` propagates every sibling `disable*` flag to both subagent factories; this one is missing from both, so a subagent of an agent that disabled knowledge context still gets the full knowledge injection.\n2. **No tests.** The diff is production-only; the PR body lists the test as \"suggested\". `WorkspaceContextMiddlewareMemoryPromptTest` is a ready-made template for exactly these assertions.\n3. **No docs.** `docs/v2/{en,zh}/docs/harness/workspace.md` tabulate every other `disable*` switch and currently state that `knowledge/` can only be switched off via `disableWorkspaceContext()`.\n\nMinor prompt-shape notes (empty `<domain_knowledge_context>` element, possibly-empty guidance block, constructor arity) are inline.\n\n### Findings\n- **[Warning]** `HarnessAgent.java:1253` — `disableKnowledgeContext` is not captured/propagated in either subagent factory in `HarnessAgentBuilderSupport`\n- **[Warning]** `HarnessAgent.java:2257` — no test coverage added for the new switch or the two new notice variants\n- **[Warning]** `HarnessAgent.java:2249-2261` — `docs/v2/en` + `docs/v2/zh` `harness/workspace.md` switch tables not updated\n- **[Info]** `WorkspaceContextMiddleware.java:194` — seventh positional param / third adjacent boolean on a public constructor; a setter would match the existing `setArtifactDeliveryEnabled` pattern\n- **[Info]** `WorkspaceContextMiddleware.java:303` — `buildGuidance()` can now return a lone `\"\\n\"`, leaving an empty guidance block in the assembled prompt\n- **[Info]** `WorkspaceContextMiddleware.java:624` — an empty `<domain_knowledge_context></domain_knowledge_context>` element is still emitted; consider skipping it like `additionalBlock`\n\n*Not blocking:* none of the above changes behaviour for callers who leave the flag off — default path is byte-identical.\n\n---\n*Automated review by github-manager-bot*",
